---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons copy -h <==
Install one client's addons on another, where builds exist (undoable)

Usage: omaddons copy [OPTIONS] --from <TARGET> --to <TARGET> [ADDON]...

Arguments:
  [ADDON]...  Only these addons of --from (names, or catalog names and aliases); default: every
              addon installed explicitly there

Options:
      --from <TARGET>  The client to copy from (one client: id, key, game mode, family, product,
                       flavor folder or path)
      --to <TARGET>    The client to install on (one client)
      --strict         Exit 6 when an addon fails to copy (skips never count)
      --no-deps        Install only the addons copied, not the ones their TOCs require on --to

Examples:
  omaddons copy --from era --to anniversary  every explicit addon of era
  omaddons copy --from era --to anniversary Questie
                                             only the addons named

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons copy --help <==
Install one client's addons on another, where builds exist (undoable)

Usage: omaddons copy [OPTIONS] --from <TARGET> --to <TARGET> [ADDON]...

Arguments:
  [ADDON]...
          Only these addons of --from (names, or catalog names and aliases); default: every addon
          installed explicitly there

Options:
      --from <TARGET>
          The client to copy from (one client: id, key, game mode, family, product, flavor folder or
          path)

      --to <TARGET>
          The client to install on (one client)

      --strict
          Exit 6 when an addon fails to copy (skips never count)

      --no-deps
          Install only the addons copied, not the ones their TOCs require on --to

Examples:
  omaddons copy --from era --to anniversary             every explicitly installed addon
  omaddons copy --from era --to anniversary Questie     only the ones named
  omaddons copy --from era --to anniversary --dry-run   what would install, what is skipped

Copies every addon installed explicitly on --from (or the ones named) to --to, in one
transaction, unpinned. Dependencies resolve on --to from its own TOCs. An addon already
there, a local file and an addon with no build for --to are skipped, never failed.

See also: install, export

Global options:
      --json              One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>   Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>   The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the
                          Classic Era client), family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every
                          client) [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run           Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change
                          nothing)
      --actor <ACTOR>     Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>     Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by
                          commands that change nothing)
      --offline           Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running     Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --if-match <TOKEN>  Change nothing unless the plan is still the one the --dry-run that
                          returned this token (data.precondition) showed
      --no-color          No ANSI color
      --no-progress       No progress output
      --progress <MODE>   Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet             Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...        More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help              Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
